  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, the VRC Animator Tracking Control only sets the state to tracking or animation when the state is entered. This forces the user for layers where the animation branches off into multiple animations to add the tracking control to every state to set it back.\n\nSince a lot of use cases for using the Animator Tracking Control is for a single state animation (as example, a closed-eye gesture should disable the blinking), it would be a cleaner and easier to manage solution if the Animator Tracking Control offered the option to only change the tracking to the specified choice while the state is active, and to set it back to the previous state when the state is exited, instead of relying on the next state to do that.",
